<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch oilseed crush down in 1996.</title>
<headline>Dutch oilseed crush down in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch oilseed firms crushed 4.72 million tonnes of seed in the whole of 1996, down almost 1.5 percent on 1995's figure of 4.79 million, the Dutch oils and fats board (MVO) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The soy crush dropped 2.6 percent to 3.9 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Unfavourable prices continued to affect the rapeseed crush, which fell 26 percent to 130,000 tonnes but conteracting this, sunflowerseed benefitted from more profitable crushing margins, pushing its crush up 15 percent to 587,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Linseed processing rose 10,000 to 87,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
